    {
      "id": 106606,
      "name": "MigrantP",
      "username": "MigrantP",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/{size}/1921_2.png",
      "created_at": "2014-06-15T01:15:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I don't see anywhere in the rules to suggest you're \"supposed to\" put tokens on opposition ships when they enter play. It's really annoying to move ships around with tokens on them, so the fewer the better.</p><p>When I play, if there's no tokens on a corner of an opposition ship, that's the current value. So I use the zero tokens to represent zero. It works well.</p><p>All of the different ways seem fine, but may make for interesting times when people who use different methods play together =)</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:36:34.145Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
