      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I don&#39;t see anywhere in the rules to suggest you&#39;re &quot;supposed to&quot; put tokens on opposition ships when they enter play. It&#39;s really annoying to move ships around with tokens on them, so the fewer the better.</p><p>When I play, if there&#39;s no tokens on a corner of an opposition ship, that&#39;s the current value. So I use the zero tokens to represent zero. It works well.</p><p>All of the different ways seem fine, but may make for interesting times when people who use different methods play together =)</p>",
